  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nHot conditions are expected throughout the forecast with highs in the \nupper 90s to low 100s each day and upper 60s to upper 70s each \nnight. There will be a persistent trough of low pressure across \nportions of western Kansas throughout the forecast in which a few \nthunderstorms may form along during peak heating. Otherwise expect \ndry conditions with winds from a southerly direction ahead of this \ntrough and east to northeast winds north of this trough. Apparent \ntemperatures look to reach towards 105 degrees this afternoon but \nhave decided with neighboring CWAs to not issue a heat advisory at \nthis time. In addition, low RHs and breezy conditions look to \nelevate fire weather risk this afternoon across central Kansas where \nwinds are stronger.",
